<h2 class="mm-heading mm-h2 mm-header-banner" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1140]" style="background-color: #2F5496; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 8pt; margin-bottom: 4pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>1</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>2</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>. PMS:</strong></span></h2>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1141]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Incidence = 40%.</strong></em></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1142]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Severe PMS = 5 – 8%.</strong></em></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1143]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">1.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Psychological Symptoms:</strong></em></span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1144]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Depression, irritability, loss of interest, mood swings, loss of confidenc</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>e – </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>due to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>serotonin + GABA receptors.</span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1145]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">2.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Physical symptoms:</strong></em></span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1146]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bloatedness,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Mastalgia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1147]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More in luteal phase.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1148]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Etiology:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1149]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Two theories </strong></span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1150]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">1.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>w</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>omen </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>with</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> PMS progesterone levels are</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> same but </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>increased </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>sensitivity</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1151]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">2.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Neurotransmitters</strong></u></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1152]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">-</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> serotonin receptors r sensitive to E &amp; P</span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1153]" style="margin-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SSRI    e</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>s</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> symptoms.</span></p>
