><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:10pt''><strong>chlamydia </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Trachomatis</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>20 – 40age.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- No Urinary symptoms.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:10pt''>Neonatal </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>conjunctivitis</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> &gt;5days.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Acute cervicitis.</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:56.15pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>15 – 19y = 1.5 – 4.3%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>50% resolve spontaneously over 12m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><sup>0</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Rectal</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 3 – 50% in MSM 70% in heterosexual.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:10pt''><u><strong>Phalangeal</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:10pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>0.5 – 2.3% MSM</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>SARA</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 1%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>PID</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 16%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Subfertility </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>1 – 20% after PID</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Periportal </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Adhesions</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>5 – 10%.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Co – infections</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" 