<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7202]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Possible adverse effects and/or consider some monitoring</strong></em></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:120.25pt;"><col style="width:382.75pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="483" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:120.25pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Drug Class</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:382.75pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Interaction</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:120.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Antihypertensives</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:382.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase BP</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> and </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>antagonize antihypertensive efficacy</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:120.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Antidiabetics</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:382.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>antagonize</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong> the </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>hypoglycemic</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong> effect</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> of antidiabetics.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:120.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Anxiolytics &amp; hypnotics</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:382.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens and progestogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>reduce plasma concentrations</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>lorazepam, oxazepam, and temazepam</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:120.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Thyroid hormones</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:382.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase the requirements for thyroid hormones</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> in hypothyroidism.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7203]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"> </p>
<h4 class="mm-heading mm-h4" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7204]" style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Increased levels or adverse effects</strong></em></span></h4>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:143.75pt;"><col style="width:380.5pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="480" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Drug Class</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:380.5pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Interaction Details</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Immunosuppressants</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:380.5pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>EE (</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Ethinylestradiol</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>) might </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase tacrolimus concentrations</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> — should be monitored by a specialist. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Ciclosporin levels</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> may be increased by estrogens and progestogens.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>UPA (Ulipristal Acetate)</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:380.5pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Predicted to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase everolimus and sirolimus concentrations</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="1075" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Dopaminergic</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:380.5pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Selegiline levels</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> may increase due to estrogens/progestogens → </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>toxicity risk</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>. EE reduces </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>ropinirole clearance</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> by ~one-third. Manufacturers advise </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>avoiding concurrent use</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7205]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"> </p>
<h4 class="mm-heading mm-h4" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7206]" style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Possible adverse effects and/or consider some monitoring</strong></em></span></h4>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:108.15pt;"><col style="width:431.35pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Drug Class</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Interaction</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Antifungals</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens and progestogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase levels of voriconazole</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Anxiolytics &amp; hypnotics</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens and progestogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase plasma concentrations</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> of chlordiazepoxide, diazepam, and clorazepate.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Bronchodilators</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>slightly reduce the clearance of theophylline</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>, leading to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increased plasma concentrations</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>. Reducing dosage is recommended if adverse effects occur.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Muscle relaxants</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Estrogens and progestogens may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>increase tizanidine levels</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> and its </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>adverse effects</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h4 class="mm-heading mm-h4" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7207]" style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Possible adverse effects and/or consider some monitoring</strong></em></span></h4>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:149.9pt;"><col style="width:389.6pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Drug Class</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Interaction</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Potassium-sparing diuretics and aldosterone antagonists</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Additive </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>hyperkaliemia</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong> or hypotension</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> might occur with </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Drosperinone</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> and potassium-sparing diuretics.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Retinoids</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Adverse effects of oral contraceptives on lipids may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>add to those of isotretinoin</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>. As retinoids are </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>teratogenic</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>, </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>highly effective contraception</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> (e.g., </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>IUDs or progestogen-only implants</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>) is recommended.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>✅</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Triptans</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>COCs (Combined Oral Contraceptives) appear to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>slightly raise levels of frovatriptan, naratriptan, and zolmitriptan</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>, though not clinically significant.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h4 class="mm-heading mm-h4" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7208]" style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt"> </h4>
<div class="mm-heading mm-h4 mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7209]" style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt; padding-left: 72pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Effect of Enzyme Inducers (during use and for 4 weeks after)</strong></em></span></span></div>', 0);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-05-013-1', 't-mm-05-013', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:202.6pt;"><col style="width:9.2pt;"><col style="width:9.2pt;"><col style="width:39.95pt;"><col style="width:38.95pt;"><col style="width:53.65pt;"><col style="width:15.4pt;"><col style="width:15.4pt;"><col style="width:59.85pt;"><col style="width:47.15pt;"><col style="width:48.15pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Drug Type</strong></span></p></td><td colspan="5" style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Impact of Enzyme Inducers</strong></span></p></td><td colspan="4" style="white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>Action</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>CHC</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> (Combined Hormonal Contraception)</span></p></td><td colspan="5" style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>❌</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> Known clinical interaction</span></p></td><td colspan="4" style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Avoid use; advise alternative method</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>POP</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Cali