<figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="a1736e7595304e07cb0b6f5c" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-07-001"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure a1736e7595304e07cb0b6f5c" viewbox="2286000 -9525 228600 314325" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="dbf7df31f5763fe67da2d67994a38300447384336fc29fb00821a20e12a6c73f"><defs><marker id="arrow-end-546106d0c1217c84e363" markerwidth="10" markerheight="7" refx="9" refy="3.5" orient="auto" markerunits="strokeWidth"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 3.5 L 0 7 Z" fill="#000000"></path></marker></defs><g data-mm-object-id="546106d0c1217c84e363" transform="translate(2408555 44378)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 0 L 1 152400" fill="none" fill-opacity="0" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700" marker-end="url(#arrow-end-546106d0c1217c84e363)"></path></g></g></svg></figure>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9963]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9964]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>8.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>Thyroid Problems:</strong></u></span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9965]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Thyroid peroxid</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>ase antibodies r associated with RPL</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>, so work up is </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>offered but thyroxine is not given in eu</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>thyroid</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> women</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>.</strong></u></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9966]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Subclinical Hypothyroidism</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> has </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>association with</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> RPL.</strong></u></span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9967]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>        </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Thyroxine supplementation:</strong></span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9968]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">1.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Not recommended routinely with mild SCH (TSH &gt;2.5).</strong></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9969]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">2.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Consider Thyroxine</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> if TSH &gt; 4Miu/l</strong></u></span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9970]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">3.</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> r</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>egular TSH test from 7 – 9weeks, until 34 weeks is recommended in case of </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>positive TPO</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> antibodies</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> and or/SCH because of risk of progression to </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>overt </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>hypothyroidism.</strong></u></span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9971]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>9.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>Progesterone supplementation:</strong></u></span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9972]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt; padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>RPL + Bleeding = Micronized</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> progesterone </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>is </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>recommended 400mg,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Plv,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> twice a day</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> from </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>b</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>leeding</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> till 16weeks</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></span></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9973]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>10</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>.Unexplained</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong> RPL</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>:</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong> </strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9974]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>should receive only supportive care in dedicated </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>RPL clinic</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>.</u></span></p>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9975]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Supportive Therapy 75% success.</span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9976]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> aspirin/ heparin not recommended</span></span></div>
<div class="mm-para mm-list-item" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9977]" style="padding-left: 36pt"><span class="mm-list-marker" aria-hidden="true">•</span><span class="mm-list-body"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> endometrial scratch test not recommended.</span></span></div>
