nt-size:12pt''><strong>1%</strong></span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:127.55pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>-</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> Empty</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> ut</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>e</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>rus</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Barr</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>el shape C</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>ervix</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- S</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>ac</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> below internal OS</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Absence of sliding sign</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Bl</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>oo</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>d flow on Co</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>l</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>or</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> Dopp</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>l</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>er</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>B – HCG:</strong></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Single – HCG to diagnose</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:160.65pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''><strong>Medical management with methotrexate: </strong></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- Success rate with local/systemic metho is 91%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- success rate decreases with beta HCG over 10000, positive fetal heart activity and gestational age &gt;12 weeks</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''><strong>Surgical management:</strong></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- More failure</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> consider for women with life threatening bleeding, failed medical </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>management or unstable patient.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- Dilatation and </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>curettage</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> or hysteroscopic resection  with or without uterine artery </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>embolization</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:159.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:106.1pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Caesarian</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong> </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Scar ectopic: </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>CSP</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Incidence</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 1/2000</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Recurrence 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.2%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 5% more if scar thickness</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> is</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> &lt;5mm.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Risk Factors:</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Previous </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>c/</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>section on breach or high uterine incision due to poorly formed lower segment</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Types:</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>1.</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>E</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>ndogenous</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>progressing</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> towards uterine cavity &amp; reaching </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>term b</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>ut risk of PPH.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>2.</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong> E</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>xogenous</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Progressing towards </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>serosa – risk of rupture &amp; </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>hem</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>p</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>eritoneum</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:127.55pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>TVS:</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong> </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>1st choice to diagnose</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>- </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Empty uterine cavity &amp; Cervical canal</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-  G.S / trophoblast mass @ scar </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>site</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-  Thin / </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>absent</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> myometrium between bladder &amp; G.S.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-  </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>placental</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"C