rker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Breathing more difficult during pregnancy.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Resp function by vital capacity.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Physiotherapy, continuous positive airway pressure CPAP, Mechanical ventilation.</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Vital capacity &lt;12 – 15ml/kg =&gt; mechanical ventilation.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Noxious stimuli =&gt; AD:</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Triggers</span></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Urinary: distention, calculi, blocked catheter, UTI.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>GI: Haemorrhoids, constipation, appendicitis,</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Skin: tight clothing, Blister, burns, ulcers.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>R.S: periods, intercourse.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Others: DVT.</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>S/S:</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Rise in B.P 20 – 40 diagnostic</span></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Nausea, vomiting, malaise, prickling sensation, thrombin headache, ringing in head.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Sweating, blushing, piloerection, tremors, nasal congestion, increased spasm.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Bradycardia, prolong PR internal AV Block disappearance of P WAVE, ventricular ECTOPIC BEATS.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Fetal bradycardia.</li></ul><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>Treatment: </strong></u></span></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Nifedipine S/L 10 – 40mg (1st line)</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>(S/L or bite &amp; swallow tablets).</span></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>GTN patch/spray.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Nitroglycerine.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Labetalol</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Hydralazine</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Avoidance of triggers</li></ul><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Hospital admission @ 36 + 6 weeks:</li></ul><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 54pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>CTG.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>U.C palpations every 4 hours.</li></ul><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Manual perception of contraction.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Bladder emptying and A/B for asymptomatic bacteriuria, </li></ul><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>ECV</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
