36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>6. Liver disease or CKD.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>7. Travelling to endemic areas.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Meningococcal </span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>1. Asplenia.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>2. Immune suppression.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>3. Complement deficiency.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>4. High risk endemics travel.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>5. University students &lt; 25 years</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> of age</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>6. Contact with infected individuals.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Pneumococcal</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>1. Asplenia.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>2. SCD.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>3. Splenectomy.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>4. HIV.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Typhoid </span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>1. Travel to endemics.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Rabies</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Post exposure prophylaxis recommended</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Pre – exposure prophylaxis – where risk of exposure to rabies is substantial.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Yellow fever</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- High case fatality.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>- Given when travel is un avoidable.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
